{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the matrix of Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen (1993). A directed graph’s edge is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"column with one source and one target, which gives the oriented incidence matrix of spectral"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L). The matrix conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Two bit planes","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Two-bit-planes"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sources and the targets are each stored as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", so a vertex can be on both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sides of a column. Its entry is then target − source = 0, with both bits kept."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sources(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"targets(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the stars and equality read the planes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so nothing is lost. A directed self-loop is such a column. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed"},{"type":"text","text":" swaps the planes, negating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every entry, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transposed()"},{"type":"text","text":" transposes each plane to give the dual. Both are O(1)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is 4·n·m\/8 bytes, so the matrix suits dense or small incidence. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sparse representation. Equality compares both planes cell for cell, with equal shape, so column"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order counts."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph. Entry (v, p) is −1 when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise."}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"role":"symbol","title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init()","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentati